  "docTitle": "Vending Machine - SDE Prep Dojo",
  "description": "Design a vending machine the way MakeMyTrip expects: five State classes, inventory, a bounded change-making DP behind a ChangeMaker strategy, refunds and admin mode, in Java, Python and C++14.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">Read 55 min</span><span class=\"chip\">Build 90 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Machine coding case</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Rank 21 of the LLD question list</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Vending Machine</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">The canonical State-pattern problem, asked at Amazon, MakeMyTrip and Swiggy: coins go in, a product and the right change come out, and every button means something different depending on what the machine is doing. You build five states, an inventory, a cash box that can run out of coins, change-making that does not fail when a greedy one would, and refunds that always give back exactly what was put in. Java, Python and C++14 code all run.</p>\n"
  },
